# Supabase connection for the browser client (A1 account features).
# Public demo: leave BOTH values empty and run npm run build:demo.
# Connected preview: copy to .env.local (ignored by Git) and fill for your project or the
# local test stack (`npx supabase start` in the repo root prints both).
# Only the public publishable/anon key belongs here — never service_role,
# secrets or database passwords.
# https://supabase.com/docs/guides/getting-started/api-keys
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Connected build: npm run build:connected (default build is disconnected demo).
# Hosted build: HTTPS origin + sb_publishable_... (or legacy anon JWT) only.
# Never prefix a server variable with VITE_. Unexpected VITE_ variables fail builds.
# Static Vite config is baked into JS at BUILD time; runtime hosting env changes
# do not update the client. Rebuild and redeploy after changing these values.
